Subject: Gives the register store its own PIC fill and an inline hit

What this does
  Gives the register store its own PIC fill and an inline hit.

Why we need it
  `put_field` had no register cache: every store took `regvm_t_put_field_slow`, and `regvm_t_put_field`'s inline hit read the stack `ic_table`, which is NULL for register code.

What it adds
  `regvm_put_pic_fill` records the post-write own writable data slot on a plain non-exotic object with a hashed shape, sharing `regvm_pic_install` with the read fill; `regvm_put_field_ic` performs the engine write and fills on success; `regvm_t_put_field` and the monolith `L_ROP_put_field` hit `REG_PIC_OWN_W` with one shape compare and write the slot, releasing the old value inline. The PIC is runtime-only, so no format, opcode or blob changed.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
